# Better GNOME Shell

GNOME Shell 50 ESM extension (`better-gnome-shell@leonardo`). It customizes the top bar and the overview Dash.

Before implementing a feature, read:

- `docs/constraints.md`
- `docs/architecture.md`
- `docs/coding-practices.md`
- `docs/patterns.md`

`AGENTS.md` is the index.

## Hard rules

- GJS only. Import from `gi://` and `resource:///`. No Node, npm, bundler, `require()`, or TypeScript.
- Shell 50 only. Do not add shims for older shells unless the task asks.
- Never edit `/usr/share/gnome-shell`. Apply changes at runtime and reverse them in `disable()`.
- `extension.js` only owns lifecycle. UI and patches go in `features/`.
- `disable()` must undo a partial `enable()` and must not throw. Remove timeouts, disconnect signals, restore methods, restore stock widgets, destroy actors this extension created, then null the fields.
- The smile indicator in `extension.js` is the template. Remove it when the first feature lands. Do not build on it.
- Dock work customizes `Main.overview.dash` unless the task explicitly asks for a persistent dock.
- Do not add a GSettings schema or `prefs.js` until a task needs a user preference.
- `prefs.js` only adds pages. Each preferences page or subpage is its own named export under `preferences/`.

New JS files start with `// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later`.
